{
 "sections": [
  {
   "title": "Chapter 3: The Country That Wasn't Allowed to Vote",
   "beats": [
    {
     "id": "s04b01",
     "shot": "geneva",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "In July 1954, international negotiations in Geneva temporarily divided Vietnam near the 17th parallel.",
     "sfx": [
      [
       "paper",
       "w:Geneva",
       0.4
      ],
      [
       "slide_down",
       "w:17th",
       0.4
      ]
     ],
     "date": 1954
    },
    {
     "id": "s04b02",
     "shot": "geneva",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "Ho Chi Minh's communist government controlled the North.",
     "date": 1954,
     "sfx": []
    },
    {
     "id": "s04b03",
     "shot": "geneva",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "An anti-communist government backed by the West controlled the South.",
     "date": 1954,
     "sfx": []
    },
    {
     "id": "s04b04",
     "shot": "geneva",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "The division was supposed to be temporary.",
     "date": 1954,
     "sfx": [
      [
       "stamp",
       "w:temporary.",
       0.5
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s04b05",
     "shot": "election",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "National elections were planned for 1956, with the aim of reunifying the country.",
     "date": 1956,
     "sfx": []
    },
    {
     "id": "s04b06",
     "shot": "election",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "But those elections never happened.",
     "date": 1956,
     "sfx": [
      [
       "stamp",
       "w:never",
       0.6
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s04b07",
     "shot": "election",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "Why?",
     "date": 1956,
     "sfx": [
      [
       "boing",
       2,
       0.4
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s04b08",
     "shot": "election",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "Because American officials believed Ho Chi Minh would probably win.",
     "date": 1956,
     "sfx": []
    },
    {
     "id": "s04b09",
     "shot": "election",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "President Dwight Eisenhower later wrote that he believed Ho could have received around 80",
     "date": 1954,
     "sfx": []
    },
    {
     "id": "s04b10",
     "shot": "election",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "percent of the vote.",
     "date": 1954,
     "sfx": [
      [
       "kaching",
       4,
       0.4
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s04b11",
     "shot": "election",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "Washington feared that a nationwide election would deliver Vietnam to the communists without another shot being fired.",
     "date": 1956,
     "sfx": []
    },
    {
     "id": "s04b12",
     "shot": "diem",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "So the United States supported South Vietnamese leader Ngo Dinh Diem and opposed reunification",
     "date": 1955,
     "sfx": []
    },
    {
     "id": "s04b13",
     "shot": "diem",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "elections that might bring Ho to power.",
     "date": 1955,
     "sfx": []
    },
    {
     "id": "s04b14",
     "shot": "diem",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "Diem was fiercely anti-communist, but his government was increasingly authoritarian.",
     "date": 1955,
     "sfx": [
      [
       "stamp",
       "w:authoritarian.",
       0.5
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s04b15",
     "shot": "diem",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "His administration favored Catholics in a predominantly Buddhist country,",
     "date": 1955,
     "sfx": []
    },
    {
     "id": "s04b16",
     "shot": "diem",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "suppressed political opponents, and alienated large parts of the population.",
     "date": 1955,
     "sfx": [
      [
       "clang",
       "w:suppressed",
       0.5
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s04b17",
     "shot": "monks",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "In 1963, Buddhist protests erupted into a major political crisis.",
     "date": 1963,
     "sfx": [
      [
       "steps",
       2,
       0.3
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s04b18",
     "shot": "monks",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "The United States had backed Diem as the man who could save South Vietnam.",
     "date": 1963,
     "sfx": [
      [
       "steps",
       2,
       0.3
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s04b19",
     "shot": "monks",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "Now it was watching him lose the support of his own people.",
     "date": 1963,
     "sfx": [
      [
       "steps",
       2,
       0.3
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s04b20",
     "shot": "coup",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "On November 1, 1963, South Vietnamese military officers overthrew his government.",
     "date": 1963,
     "sfx": [
      [
       "machine",
       2,
       0.4
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s04b21",
     "shot": "coup",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "Diem was killed the following day.",
     "date": 1963,
     "sfx": [],
     "quiet": true,
     "mood": "sombre"
    },
    {
     "id": "s04b22",
     "shot": "coup",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "American officials had quietly supported the coup, although they did not control every aspect of what followed.",
     "date": 1963,
     "sfx": [
      [
       "paper",
       4,
       0.4
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s04b23",
     "shot": "jfk",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "Just three weeks later, President John F.",
     "date": 1963,
     "sfx": [],
     "quiet": true,
     "mood": "sombre"
    },
    {
     "id": "s04b24",
     "shot": "jfk",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "Kennedy was assassinated in Dallas.",
     "date": 1963,
     "sfx": [],
     "quiet": true,
     "mood": "sombre"
    },
    {
     "id": "s04b25",
     "shot": "jfk",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "The man who had expanded America's military presence in Vietnam was gone.",
     "date": 1963,
     "sfx": [],
     "quiet": true,
     "mood": "sombre"
    },
    {
     "id": "s04b26",
     "shot": "jfk",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "But the commitment he had helped build remained.",
     "date": 1963,
     "sfx": [],
     "quiet": true,
     "mood": "sombre"
    },
    {
     "id": "s04b27",
     "shot": "advisers",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "By late 1963, the United States had roughly 16,000 military personnel in Vietnam,",
     "date": 1963,
     "sfx": [
      [
       "ticks",
       "w:16,000",
       0.4
      ]
     ],
     "amb": "birds"
    },
    {
     "id": "s04b28",
     "shot": "advisers",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "most officially serving as advisers and support staff.",
     "date": 1963,
     "sfx": [],
     "amb": "birds"
    },
    {
     "id": "s04b29",
     "shot": "advisers",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "They trained South Vietnamese forces, provided intelligence, and helped direct military operations.",
     "date": 1963,
     "sfx": [],
     "amb": "birds"
    },
    {
     "id": "s04b30",
     "shot": "unstable",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "But the South Vietnamese government remained unstable, and the communist insurgency continued to grow.",
     "date": 1963,
     "sfx": [
      [
       "pops",
       "w:insurgency",
       0.3
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s04b31",
     "shot": "unstable",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "America had spent years trying to prevent South Vietnam from falling.",
     "date": 1963,
     "sfx": []
    },
    {
     "id": "s04b32",
     "shot": "unstable",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "Now Washington faced an uncomfortable question.",
     "date": 1963,
     "sfx": []
    },
    {
     "id": "s04b33",
     "shot": "unstable",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "What happens when the government you're trying to save cannot reliably save itself?",
     "date": 1963,
     "sfx": [
      [
       "boing",
       "w:save",
       0.4
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s04b34",
     "shot": "tonkin_tease",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "The answer came in the summer of 1964.",
     "date": 1964,
     "sfx": [],
     "amb": "waves"
    },
    {
     "id": "s04b35",
     "shot": "tonkin_tease",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "And it began with a warship in the Gulf of Tonkin.",
     "date": 1964,
     "sfx": [],
     "amb": "waves"
    }
   ],
   "mood": "tension"
  }
 ]
}